delim-patterns
owner: fable-5.1 session 53f400ad
started: 2026-09-17
what: the four practical shapes of delimited control, as NAMED
  combinators rather than raw `shift`, each with the zero-type-
  argument direct spelling (the `in.Res` trick from delim-one-type):
    1. exit(value)        - leave the block early with an answer
    2. emit(a) / collect  - a push API read as a pull: the generator
    3. pause(q) / Paused / drive - stop in the middle, resume later
    4. onReturn(f)        - run the rest, then act on its answer
  Plus docs/continuations-in-practice.md: each pattern as a PAIR (how
  it is usually written / how it is written with a capture), the
  "reach for an effect first, wrap a shift in a name last" rule with
  its reasons, and the section on when a capture makes code worse
  (multi-shot with vars, resources under a captured k, stack traces).
files: src/main/scala/Delim.scala, src/test/scala/TestDelimPatterns.scala,
  docs/continuations-in-practice.md, docs/theory/02-continuations.md,
  CHANGELOG.md
